{"id": "EUVD-2016-10917", "enisaUuid": "2c345d65-c43d-3855-b915-9e4b2ca95a52", "description": "Memphis Documents Library plugin for WordPress before 3.1.6 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files via the mdocs-img-preview parameter. Attackers can send GET requests with traversal sequences to mdocs_img_preview() in mdocs-downloads.php to download wp-config.php containing database credentials. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-22.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T20:31:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T02:10:01", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/39593", "https://packetstorm.news/files/id/136374/", "https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/53999c06-05ca-44f1-b713-1e4d6b4a3f9f", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/wp-memphis-documents-library-lfi.yaml", "https://wordpress.org/plugins/memphis-documents-library/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/memphis-documents-library-wordpress-plugin-3.1.6-path-traversal-via-mdocs-img-preview"], "aliases": ["CVE-2016-20100", "GHSA-322h-ww5h-3m7g"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d9b528c5-cc25-3464-8f69-a3318dddc740", "product": {"name": "Memphis Documents Library", "vendor": {"name": "Ian Howatson"}}, "product_version": "2.2.1 <3.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9537e9ad-6c60-3b72-b78f-9bdd5cfd4ab6", "vendor": {"name": "Ian Howatson"}}], "isExploited": false}